# Git commit messages

When the user asks to commit, write messages a reviewer can scan without opening the diff.

## Subject (required)

- Imperative, present tense: `Add`, `Fix`, `Cap`, `Scope` — not `Added` / `Fixes` / `Updated files`
- One line, ~72 characters, no trailing period
- Lead with **why** or **user-visible outcome**, not a file list
- Optional Conventional Commits prefix when it matches this repo: `feat:`, `fix:`, `perf:`, `test:`, `docs:`, `chore:`
- Scope in parentheses when it narrows the area: `fix(leave):`, `perf(recruitment):`

## Body (when the diff is not obvious)

- Blank line after the subject
- 1–4 short lines: motivation, constraint, or risk (migration, env, rollout)
- Do not repeat the subject or paste a file dump

## Split commits

- One logical change per commit (auth gate ≠ Prisma pool ≠ leave idempotency)
- Do not squash unrelated work into `Update stuff` or `WIP`
- Skip secrets (`.env`, credentials). Warn if the user asks to include them
- Skip scratch files (`scripts/_tmp-*`, `*.tsbuildinfo`) unless the user asks

## Examples

```
# ❌ BAD
Update prisma and auth
fix bugs
WIP
```

```
# ✅ GOOD
fix(db): cap Prisma pool per ECS task to protect RDS connections

feat(auth): block local users until they change a required password

fix(leave): make ledger writes idempotent under concurrent approval
```
